The user requires Claude review instructions only when items were added to git span notes since the last stop (chat requirement, 2026-10-22). Notes IDs increase monotonically within the store in the shared Git common directory, even after removal of every note; Claude checkpoints therefore bind the highest observed ID to the canonical common-directory path, not the current worktree root or commit SHA. Linked worktrees share the observation boundary, while another note added on the same commit remains new. The linked-worktree and same-commit tests cover these distinctions; resetting or replacing a notes database during a live session is outside this checkpoint contract.
